 ## Overview
-This method renders cloud surfaces in regimes where the diffusion approximation is invalid, specifically at cloud edges where single scattering and low-order multiple scattering break directional independence [S1, unofficial]. It solves this by using hierarchical volume rendering with opacities $\rho(X)\sigma_t$ and voxel colors $I_0(X)$, selecting view-dependent octree cubes based on projected area-weighted approximation errors [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from standard octree volume rendering by its specific use of least-squares approximations for color and opacity combined with a hardware cell-projection compositing step [S1, unofficial].
